# Session report

End every user-facing reply with two short lines, after the work:

- **Learned:** the choice just made, in one or two sentences. Name the file or the clock when there is one. If this turn changed nothing, say the standing lesson that still applies.
- **Could adjust:** one open knob. A duration, a land, a chain setting, or a file not yet recut. Do not invent a second project.

When the choice should survive the chat, write it the same day into the skill it belongs to, `USER.md`, or `planning/instincts/` with the date. A reply is not a lesson until that write exists.

Standing choices from 2026-10-26, until a later pass replaces them:

- A short has a theme: the chance the audience is given. 13-sh02 (02:27–03:21) is the chance to consider making a decision against taking one. The definition of that pair is 13-sh13.
- Lecture-cut posts can take a pair: one prescheduled file from the long video, then a live he does right after to elaborate and reflect. The live is the connection. It is not a second Sheet row.
- Same register. Do not splice a confession onto a later list. Lecture 13: 13-sh02 is 02:27–03:21. 13-sh12 is the clarity list, 05:06–06:00.
- A change of vibe is not the missing context for another short. Mom is the example in 13-sh13 (11:01–12:04), land "taken from the environment." She is not the setup for 13-sh02.
- Voice is de-esser, presence EQ, `loudnorm` −16 / LRA 11. No compressor, no `dynaudnorm`. Trim stays off while `auto-editor` will not start.
